// Title: Remote Access Tool - ScreenConnect Server Web Shell Execution
// Sigma ID: b19146a3-25d4-41b4-928b-1e2a92641b1b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Jason Rathbun (Blackpoint Cyber)
// Date: 2024-02-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: initial-access, T1190
// Description: Detects potential web shell execution from the ScreenConnect server process.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://blackpointcyber.com/resources/blog/breaking-through-the-screen/
//   - https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/security-bulletins/connectwise-screenconnect-23.9.8
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_screenconnect_webshell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ScreenConnect.Service.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\csc.exe")
